## Day 2 — Event Loop + Promises + Async

### Part 1: Event Loop (deeper)

**Question 1 — What happens in this order?**
```js
console.log("1");
setTimeout(() => console.log("2"), 0);
Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log("3"));
console.log("4");
```

### Part 2: Promises

**Question 2 — What does each return and when?**
```js
Promise.all([Promise.resolve(1), Promise.reject(2), Promise.resolve(3)])
  .then(r => console.log(r))
  .catch(e => console.log(e));
```

**Question 3 — What's the output?**
```js
const p = new Promise((resolve) => {
  console.log("A");
  resolve("B");
  console.log("C");
});
p.then(v => console.log(v));
console.log("D");
```

**Question 4 — Fix this bug:**
```js
async function fetchData() {
  const res = await fetch("https://api.example.com/data");
  const data = res.json(); // what's wrong here?
  return data;
}
```

**Question 5 — What does this print?**
```js
async function foo() {
  console.log("A");
  const p = new Promise(res => res("B"));
  console.log("B");
  return p;
}
foo().then(console.log);
console.log("C");
```

