> `foo()` runs synchronously until it hits `return p`. That logs A, B. Then `.then(console.log)` is queued as a microtask. Then `console.log("C")` runs. THEN microtasks run → "B".
>
> The key: **`foo()` doesn't pause at `.then`** — `.then` is called AFTER `foo()` returns. The function body runs to completion first.

