### `new Promise` syntax explained

```js
const p = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
  // THIS CODE RUNS IMMEDIATELY (synchronously)
  // When something succeeds: resolve(value)
  // When something fails: reject(error)
});

// .then() is always async — runs after sync code finishes
p.then(value => console.log(value));
