console.log("I run first because .then() is async");
p.then(v => console.log(v)); // runs LAST
```
**Output:** `I run RIGHT NOW → I also run RIGHT NOW → I run first because .then() is async → done`

The key: **the Promise executor is just a regular function**. `resolve()` doesn't stop execution — it just tells the Promise "whenever `.then()` runs, give it this value."

